      "C": "Because $\\angle C=90^{\\circ}$, the hypotenuse is $AB=c$ opposite $C$, so $a^{2}+b^{2}=c^{2}$.",
      "D": "Also apply $a^{2}+b^{2}=c^{2}$ unchanged to every acute triangle with sides $a$, $b$, and $c$, beyond right-angled triangles."
